  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby approved shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans with the approved plans which forms part of this notice. \r \rLocation Plan; Block Plan; Highway impact assessment; SuDS proforma; P00; P01; P02; P03; P04; P05; P06; P07 (all plans dated 25/08/2026).\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning. \r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the kitchen/dining room shall be retained as such, in accordance with the approved plans, in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the cycle parking spaces proposed have been fully constructed in accordance with the hereby approved details and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.  \r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport. \r",
    "Prior to occupation of the development hereby permitted, the refuse and recycling storage hereby approved shall be provided in accordance with the approved details and thereafter maintained unless otherwise submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets. \r\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture those specified in the approved application. \r \rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area. \r",
    "The communal areas shown on the approved plans, including the communal living room at loft level, shall be retained as shared communal accommodation and shall not be used as sleeping accommodation or as additional space for individual bedrooms. These areas shall remain accessible at all times to all residents of the House in Multiple Occupation (HMO).\r \r \rReason: To ensure the provision and retention of adequate communal facilities for the benefit of all occupiers of the HMO and to maintain a satisfactory standard of residential accommodation."
  ],
